# Watching a path for changes. The clean uniform interface, the per-env native implementation selected at build
# time and hidden.
#
# THE SHAPE IS PULL, NOT CALLBACK. `watch` starts the watcher, `next` awaits the next change, `close` stops it:
#
#   save eye, call watch(read path, true)
#   save change, call next(read eye)
#
# A callback shape reads better on node and cannot be written on the other three: it would need a `task` value to
# cross into a platform thread on rust, swift and kotlin alike. Pull is the shape all four hold, so the API is the
# same everywhere rather than nearly the same. `next` on a closed watcher answers with the empty event, so a loop
# over it ends instead of hanging.
#
# A watch the host refuses raises `failure`, its note node's own message (`ENOENT: no such file or directory, watch
# '<path>'`), on every backend (term-self-host-001-1519): each backend's watch-open keeps the refusal on the platform
# handle, as the code name, the step and the host text, and `watch` raises it through file/failure. A path is refused
# where node's fs.watch refuses it: missing (ENOENT), under a file (ENOTDIR), or one the run may not read (EACCES).

mark unstable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/file/asynchronous
  find watch-open
  find watch-next
  find watch-close
  find watch-refusal
  find watch-dock

load @term/base/file/failure
  find raise-file-failure

# one change: what happened (<create>, <remove>, <change>, or <other> for a platform event with no equivalent),
# and the path it happened to. An empty `kind` means the watcher is closed and nothing more is coming.
form watch-event
  link kind, like text
  link path, like text

# a running watcher: the platform watch handle, private, plus the path it was opened on
form watcher
  link dock
    like watch-dock
  link path, like text

# start watching `path`. With `deep`, everything beneath it too. Raises `failure` when the host refuses the watch.
task watch
  mark async
  take path, like text
  take
    deep
    like boolean
    fall false
  like watcher
  save opened
    call watch-open
      read path
      read deep
  save refusal
    call watch-refusal
      read opened
  call raise-file-failure
    read refusal
    read path
  send back, read opened

# the next change. Waits until one happens, or answers with the empty event once the watcher is closed.
task next
  mark async
  take watcher, like watcher
  like watch-event
  send back
    call watch-next
      read watcher

# stop watching, releasing the platform handle
task close
  mark async
  take watcher, like watcher
  like void
  call watch-close
    read watcher
